  "dedupRule": "381 distinct OBJ-* identifiers extracted; only the 99 numeric OBJ-NNN cards are canonical objects -- the rest are mnemonic pointers into the same 99 concepts (e.g. OBJ-SURFACE, OBJ-SSO) and are not additional objects. Status is computed from the built route tree, never from a list: 7 of 99 rows read demonstrated-in-storyboard because a shipped route screen under app/ (a directory holding a page.tsx) names that exact identifier as a whole token -- the same evidence class the module rule above uses, widened from MOD-* to this family. Naming includes naming an identifier to record that the screen does NOT act on it, which this build has no structural marker to separate. Only the numeric OBJ-NNN card id counts here: the built screens overwhelmingly cite the mnemonic pointers (OBJ-SA-SESSION, OBJ-DOH-SHIFT) into the same concepts, and the source publishes no mnemonic-to-card mapping to join them on without inventing one. Every other row reads not-represented, which means no route demonstrates it AND no route mounts it -- a module may be fully built and still read not-represented if nothing has mounted it yet. Delete or rename the route that carries that evidence and those rows fall back on the next build. Studio object gaps (D11), 3 of them, registered as a GAP LIST and deliberately NOT as rows: minting OBJ-100..OBJ-102 for these would inflate a ninety-nine the source closes (R23), so the count above stays 99 and the gap is stated instead of papered over. OBJ-STU-QUALREQ -- MOD-STU-13 Qualification Requirements, card L33604-L33782 (objects-affected L33653); no numeric row because the numeric register's nearest row is OBJ-031 \"Qualification\" (L8418, owned by SURF-DOH) -- the certification a worker holds, not the requirement a Workflow states, so it is a different object and not a numeric counterpart. OBJ-STU-CAPSTATE -- MOD-STU-15 The Agent Builder, card L33961-L34153 (objects-affected L34028); no numeric row because the numeric register carries no capability, enablement or entitlement object at all, so there is no row to map onto. OBJ-STU-LOCALE -- MOD-STU-17 Localisation, card L34351-L34499 (objects-affected L34391); no numeric row because the numeric register's nearest row is OBJ-051 \"Locale pack\" (L8875, owned by SURF-SA) -- platform-side locale-pack governance, not the per-locale authored variant held inside one Workflow, so it is a different object and not a numeric counterpart. All three were found independently by three different Studio module tasks, and all three declined to mint a number.",
  "sourceFixesNoTotal": false,
